faqs:
  - q: "How do you convert text case online?"
    a: "Paste your text into the converter box and click any case transformation button such as UPPERCASE, lowercase, Title Case, or Sentence case. The text updates immediately in your browser."
  - q: "What is the difference between Title Case and Capitalize Each Word?"
    a: "Title Case capitalizes primary words but keeps minor grammatical articles and prepositions (such as 'in', 'the', 'of', 'and', 'for') in lowercase unless they appear as the first or last word. Capitalize Each Word unconditionally capitalizes the first letter of every single word."
  - q: "What is the difference between camelCase, PascalCase, snake_case, and kebab-case?"
    a: "camelCase starts lowercase and capitalizes subsequent words with no spaces (e.g. 'myVariable'). PascalCase capitalizes all words including the first ('MyVariable'). snake_case separates words with underscores in lowercase ('my_variable'). kebab-case separates words with hyphens ('my-variable')."
  - q: "Can I undo a conversion if I don't like the result?"
    a: "Yes. Click the Undo button to revert to your previous text state at any time."
  - q: "Is my text data private when using the converter?"
    a: "Yes. All text transformation logic executes strictly in local browser memory via client-side JavaScript. Your text is never stored in URLs, never saved to cookies, and never sent to remote servers."
